course: dictionary
lesson: 10446
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. Those words are the context, and they give you clues.
explain: «Blow your own trumpet» does not mean you should play a brass instrument. It is a phrase that means to boast, which is to talk proudly about yourself. Its meaning is not the same as its separate words.
explain: Trumpet can be a noun (the instrument, or the call it makes) or a verb (an action, such as to tell everyone about something proudly). Ask yourself: is it a thing, or is it something someone does?
fact: A trumpet is a brass instrument. You blow into it and press valves to change the note.
fact: «The trumpet call is air blasted out through the trunk» shows that an elephant trumpets by blowing air through its trunk.
fact: To trumpet something means to tell everyone about it proudly, and it can be a verb with forms like trumpeted and trumpeting.
fact: Trumpets are brass, not woodwind, because the sound starts when the player's lips buzz.
exercise: In «play the trumpet», what kind of word is trumpet? | A verb, meaning to boast | A verb, an action word | *A noun, the name of an instrument | An adjective, a describing word
exercise: Dad says, «Stop blowing your own trumpet!» What does he mean? | Stop playing your brass instrument so loudly | *Stop boasting about yourself | Stop making loud noises with your mouth | Stop blowing into a cup
exercise: «The trumpet call is air blasted out through the trunk.» What makes the trumpet call? | Drums beaten by the feet | *Air blasted out through the trunk | Water sucked up the trunk | A sound from a passing bus
test: In «Look up in winter and you may hear cranes' trumpet calls from kilometres away», what does trumpet call mean? | A tube for drinking | A trumpet-shaped flower | A brass musical instrument | *A loud, high call made by a bird
test: Which sentence uses trumpet as a verb meaning to boast? | *She trumpeted her win to the whole school | The elephant's trumpet was loud | He bought a new trumpet case | She carried her trumpet to band practice
exam: A trumpet is blown into, and its valves are pressed; what do the valves do? | They stop the instrument from making any sound | *They change the note | They keep the player's lips warm | They make the bell shine
